@startuml activation
title Companion to M-DP3: service activation and bounded operator maintenance (§11)
actor "Operator" as O
participant "Dispatcher service\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Durable state\njournal, effects, claims, maintenance progress" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; exec.stop and absence evidence" as H
participant "Service installer / manager" as I
== initial activation, slice 0 ==
I -> D : install/start Unix-socket service; admission closed
D -> J : exclusive state; validate compatibility; replay journal
D -> D : reconcile effects, receipts and process evidence
alt recovery unresolved / unknown / contradictory
  D -> D : remain unready; refuse admission without fallback
else recovery resolved
  D -> D : publish readiness; open admission
end
== bounded maintenance attempt ==
O -> D : explicit authorized maintenance with selected executions
note over O,D : Authorization, deadline/progress and restart-review encoding remain unpublished (§16).
D -> D : close new admission
D -> J : durable inventory and selected-stop intent
loop selected affected executions, within maintenance attempt deadline
  D -> J : journal stop intent with stable effect ID
  D -> H : exec.stop through dispatcher's authority; generation + execution identity
  alt stop refused / unknown or process absence unconfirmed
    D -> J : preserve unresolved stop and claim; defer maintenance
  else confirmed no execution process remains
    H --> D : termination receipt
    D -> J : record absence/outcome; reconcile effects/receipts
  end
end
alt deadline exhausted / incomplete reconciliation / any affected process not confirmed absent
  D -> D : defer with admission closed; no mode/schema/binary change
  D --> O : durable progress and unresolved obligations for review/resumption
else all affected executions confirmed absent and reconciled
  D -> J : retain standing allocations and identities; persist intended restarts for review
  D -> I : exclusive state ownership; validate reader/writer compatibility
  I -> I : admitted backend-mode / mutable-state migration / binary swap
  I -> D : start selected compatible service with admission closed
  D -> J : recover/reconcile; retain all later durable records
  alt recovery / compatibility unresolved
    D -> D : remain closed; rollback uses same absence and compatibility fences
  else recovery resolved
    D -> D : publish readiness; open admission
  end
end
opt operator-reviewed restart
  O -> D : fresh authority and admitted plan/transport
  D -> D : fresh prepare/start checks, including revocation.check
  D -> D : start only admitted rows; unsupported rows remain visibly stopped
end
note over D,J
  Maintenance deadline bounds the attempt, never standing execution lifetime.
  No standing retirement/identity revocation, automatic expiry or live adoption.
  Queue drain alone never stops executions. No snapshot rollback repair.
  Native resume is gated by §12; no seamless continuation is promised.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#11-installation-and-activation §11 activation/maintenance]] / §§7, 8.1, 16
endlegend
@enduml
